course: dictionary
lesson: 8183
title: Respond: answer, react or get better
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word respond has three main meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to pick. It can mean to answer, to react, or to start getting better. «The teacher asked a question, and Maya was quick to respond.» A question is something you answer, so respond means answer here.
explain: «Plants have no ears, but they can respond to vibrations.» Here respond means to react: the plant changes because something happens around it. Ask yourself: is someone answering, or is something reacting? That question helps you choose the meaning.
explain: The noun is response, so a response is an answer or a reaction. «When responding to another team, you begin with what was good in their view, then add to it or question it respectfully.» Responding here means answering another team's ideas. Swap in answer, check the sentence still makes sense, and you have your meaning.
fact: Respond means to answer, by speaking or writing.
fact: Respond can also mean to react to something by doing something.
fact: Respond to treatment means to start getting better.
fact: Verb forms: respond, responds, responded, responding. Noun: response.
fact: «Our pupils respond to bright light» means the pupils of your eyes change size when light gets brighter.
exercise: «The teacher asked a question, and Maya was quick to respond.» What does respond mean here? | *Answer | Hide the book | Fall asleep | Run away
exercise: «Plants have no ears, but they can respond to vibrations.» What does respond mean here? | *React by changing, because something happens near them | Sing a song to the wind | Write a letter to the soil | Stop growing for ever
exercise: Which word is the noun form of respond? | repeat | *response | respect | responsible
test: «The emergency services respond quickly when someone calls 999.» What does respond mean here? | *Answer the call and come to help | Argue with the caller | Go to sleep | Forget the call
test: «The patient began to respond well to the new treatment.» What does respond mean here? | Wrote a long story | Stopped talking | *Started getting better | Got worse on purpose
exam: «A sore arm after a jab is a sign the immune system is responding.» What does responding mean here? | Going to sleep early | Refusing the jab for ever | *Reacting, as the body's defences work | Answering a letter from the doctor
